    <tei:body>
      <tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/text/vayekhulu" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n36.jpg">
        <j:conditional xml:id="kiddush_vayekhulu_condition">
          <tei:note type="instruction" xml:lang="en">(On Sabbath)</tei:note>
          <j:all>
            <tei:fs type="opensiddur:holiday-aggregate">
              <tei:f name="shabbat">
                <tei:binary value="true"/>
              </tei:f>
            </tei:fs>
          </j:all>
        </j:conditional>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="chapter" n="1"/><tei:milestone unit="half-verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/1/31/b" n="b"/><tei:seg source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/1/31/b">It was evening and it was morning, the sixth day.</tei:seg> <tei:milestone unit="half-verse"/><tei:milestone unit="chapter"/><tei:milestone unit="chapter" n="2" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/2"/><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/2/1" n="1"/>The heavens and the earth were completed and all their hosts. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/2/2" n="2"/>God completed by the seventh day His work that He had done and on the seventh day He ceased from all his work which He had done. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/2/3" n="3"/>And God blessed the seventh day and sanctified it, for on it did He cease from all His work which God as Creator had done. <tei:milestone unit="verse"/><tei:milestone unit="chapter"/></tei:p>
        <j:endConditional target="#kiddush_vayekhulu_condition"/>
      </tei:div>
    </tei:body>
